## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design idempotent, serverless onboarding with minimal IAM surface, a common beginner-safe pattern.

## Key Concepts
- Idempotent operations; DynamoDB conditional/transactional writes
- Least-privilege IAM for Lambda
- CloudWatch metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Node.js Lambda outline for idempotent signup
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const ddb = new AWS.DynamoDB.DocumentClient();
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const { userId, email, transactionId } = JSON.parse(event.body);
  const params = {
    TransactItems: [
      {
        Put: {
          TableName: 'Signups',
          Item: { userId, email, signupAt: Date.now() },
          ConditionExpression: 'attribute_not_exists(userId)'
        }
      },
      {
        Put: {
          TableName: 'SignupsDedup',
          Item: { transactionId, userId },
          ConditionExpression: 'attribute_not_exists(transactionId)'
        }
      }
    ]
  };
  await ddb.transactWrite(params).promise();
  return { statusCode: 200, body: JSON.stringify({ success: true }) };
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle cold starts or retries that occur during a transaction?
- How would you test this in a CI/CD pipeline and observe idempotent behavior?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests proficiency designing fine-grained, scalable access controls for multi-tenant data lakes using ABAC, tags, and policy syntax.

## Key Concepts
- IAM tags and aws:PrincipalTag
- Resource policies with aws:RequestTag and stringEquals conditions
- S3 bucket prefixes per tenant and least privilege
- Testing cross-tenant access and tag revocation

## Code Example
```json
// Trust policy (IAM role)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT:role/TenantAccess"},
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"}}
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
// Permission policy
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::data-lake/${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}/*",
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"aws:RequestTag/tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"}}
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
// Bucket policy (alternative strict guard)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT:role/TenantAccess"},
      "Action": "s3:GetObject",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::data-lake/${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}/*",
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"s3:ExistingObjectTag/tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you rotate tags and ensure no stale access remains?
- How would you integrate with CI to validate policies in a sandbox before prod?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design scalable, auditable data-lake isolation using Lake Formation, IAM tagging, and cross-account roles; also assesses policy drafting and test planning.

## Key Concepts

- Lake Formation permissions and data location mapping
- IAM tags and condition keys
- Cross-account roles and trust policies
- S3 tenant prefixes and data encryption with KMS
- Admin audit paths and automated tests

## Code Example

```json
{
  "PolicySnippet": {
    "Version": "2012-10-17",
    "Statement": [
      {
        "Effect": "Allow",
        "Action": ["s3:GetObject","s3:PutObject"],
        "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::corp-data-lake/tenant-id/*",
        "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"aws:RequestTag/tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"}}
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

```json
{
  "LFPolicySnippet": {
    "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT:role/TenantRole"},
    "Permissions": ["SELECT","DESCRIBE","ALTER"],
    "DataLocation": "arn:aws:s3:::corp-data-lake/tenant-id/"
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test policy changes without impacting production data?
- What are the trade-offs of Lake Formation vs direct IAM/S3 controls in this scenario?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ABAC, cross-account trust, per-tenant encryption, and test rigor for production-grade data lakes.

## Key Concepts
- ABAC with IAM tags and S3 object tags
- Per-tenant KMS CMKs and encryption context
- Cross-account role with least privilege
- Test plan including canaries and revocation

## Code Example
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject","s3:ListBucket"],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::telemetry-lake/tenant-id=${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}/*"
      ],
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "s3:ExistingObjectTag/tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["kms:Decrypt","kms:Encrypt","kms:GenerateDataKey*"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:kms:region:acct:key/<tenant-id-CMK-arn>",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "kms:EncryptionContext:tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```
